 "why_this_matters": [
  "the 'official NFL Game Book' the owner's brief names as the source for actual starters and game-day status is not a hypothetical: it is one dated PDF per fixture, linked from the game centre, and it prints the lineups and the Not Active lists",
  "it is published AFTER the game, because it contains final statistics, so it is a LABEL source for backtests and for the availability graph's 'who actually did' half - never a pre-kickoff feature",
  "it carries the roof/surface and game-day weather in the header, so a totals model can be graded against actual conditions without an external weather join - but only retrospectively",
  "it does NOT print a depth order, so '2nd/3rd/4th string' still has no official source; what it does give is a starter/no-starter fact per slot per game, which is the observable half of the deficiency question"
 ]
